{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.NormalizedSumTelescopeBridge","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.hconv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.hconv","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HconvConventionBridge.lean#L107-L154","doc":"**The per-λ convention bridge `hconv`.** `q^{−κ_λ}/hookProd_q(λ) = schurElement(q²,0,λ)·(1−q²)^{|λ|}`,\nfor a weakly-decreasing partition `λ` in the substrate regime `1 < q`. This is the last unproved input\nof the telescope closure `NormalizedSumClosure.normalizedSum_eq_one_of_convBridge`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.schurElement_zero_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.schurElement_zero_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HconvConventionBridge.lean#L91-L105","doc":"**`schurElement` at `X = 0` as `q^{2n(λ)}` over the Macdonald denominator product.**\n`schurElement(q²,0,λ) = (q²)^{n(λ)} · (∏_x (1 − q^{2 h_x}))⁻¹` (the `1 − X·Q^c` numerators are `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.denomProd_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.denomProd_factor","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HconvConventionBridge.lean#L53-L89","doc":"**The Macdonald denominator product factorises.** `∏_x (1 − q^{2 h_x})` over the cells of `λ`\nequals `(−1)^{|λ|} · q^{Σh} · (q−q⁻¹)^{|λ|} · hookProd_q(λ)`, cell by cell via the per-cell brick\n`one_sub_qsq_pow_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.hookProd_eq_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.hookProd_eq_prod","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HconvConventionBridge.lean#L44-L51","doc":"**`hookProd` as a double `Finset.prod`.** The nested `foldl` of `qBracket`-of-hook is the\nrow×column cell product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.map_range_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HconvConventionBridge.map_range_prod","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HconvConventionBridge.lean#L35-L42","doc":"`((List.range n).map f).prod = ∏ i ∈ range n, f i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}